<title>BELGIUM: SGB says share undervalued.</title>
<headline>SGB says share undervalued.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian holding company Societe Generale de Belgique SA (SGB) said on Wednesday its share price was trading on the bourse at a discount to its value and this was not justified.</p>
<p>&quot;In view of the steady increase in profits over the past five years, the prospects of future profits based on a clear strategy, the stature of the group's managers and the refocusing of the portfolio on the key particiapting interests, the SGB ordinary share should not be trading at the current market discount,&quot; SGB said in a statement.</p>
<p>It gave no estimate of what the company considered its correct market value.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
